<title>USA: USDA revises 1995 livestock slaughter totals.</title>
<headline>USDA revises 1995 livestock slaughter totals.</headline>
<text>
<p>Est weekly and year to date livestock slaughter - USDA</p>
<p>					   CATTLE     CALVES	 HOGS</p>
<p>Friday     12/27/96  (est)	128,000	7,000     371,000</p>
<p>Saturday   12/28/96  (est)	 98,000	    0     173,000</p>
<p>Week ago (est)			 57,000	    0	25,000</p>
<p>Year ago (act)			 88,000	    0     222,000</p>
<p>Week to date (est)		  525,000     26,000   1,398,000</p>
<p>Same Period Last Week (est)     685,000     30,000   1,740,000</p>
<p>Same Period Last Year* (act)   *598,000*   *27,000  *1,671,000</p>
<p>1996 Year to date		35,463,000  1,690,000  89,871,000</p>
<p>1995 Year to date*	   * 34,877,000 *1,393,000 *94,201,000</p>
<p>Percent change			   1.6%	21.3%	 -4.6%</p>
<p>Note: ***1995 year totals were officially revised by USDA. 1996 Totals are subject to revision.</p>
<p>Yearly totals may not add due to rounding.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
